- How does the strategy change if you add a fourth constraint with nested S(C)?
- Can you formalize a small solver that automatically finds such assignments?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to reason with Kleene three-valued logic in a small constraint system and to design backtracking propagation that respects non-classical truth tables.

## Key Concepts

- Kleene three-valued logic with T>U>F
- Implication defined as ¬a ∨ b
- Propagation and backtracking in 3-valued CSPs

## Code Example

```javascript
function neg(x){ return x==="T"?"F": x==="F"?"T":"U"; }
function or(a,b){ return (a==="T"||b==="T")?"T": (a==="U"||b==="U")?"U":"F"; }
function and(a,b){ return (a==="F"||b=="F")?"F": (a==="U"||b==="U")?"U":"T"; }
function implies(a,b){ // ¬a ∨ b
  const na = neg(a);
  return or(na,b);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you extend to a 5-variable horizon with temporal operators like Next (X) under Kleene semantics?
- Implement a forward-checking heuristic to prune values early; what ordering helps most?

